# Implementations — Rhyme-SM3

## Directory Structure

```
Implementations/
├── Reference_Implementation/
│   ├── Rhyme-SM3-128/   (portable C99, SM3 backend)
│   ├── Rhyme-SM3-256/
│   ├── Rhyme-SM3-384/
│   └── Rhyme-SM3-512/
├── Optimized_Implementation/
│   ├── Rhyme-SM3-128/   (-march=native, incremental SM3-XOF, DP1 target)
│   ├── Rhyme-SM3-256/
│   ├── Rhyme-SM3-384/
│   ├── Rhyme-SM3-512/
│   └── README
├── Additional_Implementation/
│   └── README
└── README
```

## Reference_Implementation

Portable C99, `-DRHYME_NO_AES`.  Hash/XOF: SM3/SM3-KDF via `sm3_xof.c` →
API_PKC `pseudoXOF()`.  Wrapper layer: `rhyme_xof.c/h`.  No fips202.

## Optimized_Implementation

`-O3 -march=native`.  Two optimizations:

1. **Incremental SM3-XOF** — block-by-block generation via `sm3hash()`.
   KAT byte-identical to Reference.

2. **DP1 Fast Keygen** (`make fast`) — truncated-minor coprimality check.
   ~8-14x faster keygen; KAT differs but signatures self-verify.

| Target | Binary | KAT vs Reference |
|--------|--------|-----------------|
| `make` | `KAT_SIG` | byte-identical |
| `make fast` | `KAT_SIG_FAST` | differs (DP1, valid) |

## Common Files

`api.h` — public API parameters
`SIG_AlgorithmInstance.c/h` — API_PKC SIG wrapper
`KAT_SIG.c` — KAT driver
`auxfunc.c/h`, `drng.c/h` — API_PKC no-modify files (byte-identical to template)
`rhyme_xof.c/h` — Rhyme-specific Hash/XOF wrappers (SM3 backend)
`sm3_xof.c/h` — SM3-XOF state machine
`sm3.c/h` — thin wrappers over API_PKC sm3hash/pseudoXOF
`include/` — public headers
`src/` — core algorithm implementation (no fips202)
